  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.6pt, 789.84pt, "11 ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 82.08pt, "integrating sphere, while temperature-dependent spectral infrared emissivity is measured with ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 102.72pt, "a Fourier-transform spectrometer (Thermo Scientific, Nicolet iS50) and a reflection accessory ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 123.6pt, "(Harrick Scientific, Seagull). Samples are heated with home-made temperature stages made of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 144.24pt, "thermoelectric module, water block and PID controller. Both solar and infrared spectra are ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.88pt, "measured at every 5°C from 25°C to 60°C for the insulating phase, every 2°C from 60°C to ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 185.52pt, "80°C within the phase transition, and every 5°C from 60°C to 95°C for the metallic phase ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 206.4pt, "upon both heating and cooling. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 233.04pt, "Outdoor measurements")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(183.124pt, 233.04pt, ": Samples sit on the top surface of a 16-TEG stack (DigiKey, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 253.68pt, "MGM250-31-10-16) inside the vacuum chamber with about 5 mm spacing to the viewport. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 274.32pt, "All the interfaces are filled with thermal paste to minimize contact thermal resistance. The ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 295.2pt, "outdoor tests in vacuum use Quartz and ZnSe viewports respectively during daytime and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 315.84pt, "nighttime, and tests start after 1-hr pumping until the pressure reaches below 0.01 Pa. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 336.48pt, "Ambient tests are conducted with the same setup by replacing viewports with thin ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 357.12pt, "polyethylene films for shielding the dust and wind. The entire setup is tilted by 20° towards ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 378pt, "south only at daytime. The sample temperature is measured with a thermistor (Amphenol, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 398.64pt, "SC30F103V) during daytime and by an infrared camera (FLIR, E8-XT) after careful ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 419.28pt, "calibration at nighttime.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.767pt, 415.2pt, "[48]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.095pt, 419.28pt, " The bottom side of TEG stacks is maintained at ambient ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 439.92pt, "temperature by sitting on a water block with running water to a reservoir in thermal ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 460.8pt, "equilibrium with ambient. The temperatures of TEG stack bottom side, water block and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 481.44pt, "vacuum chamber wall are measured by thermistors with difference less than 2°C. Current-")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 502.08pt, "voltage curves from the TEG stack are collected with a source meter (Keithley 2400), and the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 522.72pt, "TEG power density is calculated as the product of voltage and current normalized to the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 543.6pt, "radiative coating surface area. Solar irradiance is measured by a pyranometer placed on the ")
